{
  "title": "Normalize: Re-extract photo imports by reading their photos again",
  "description": "Re-extract on a recipe imported from photos (POST /api/import/photos) only re-parses the extract_recipe output its import job stored: scraping::stored_source finds that output and the normalize job starts at parse_ingredients, so a better vision model or prompt never reaches old imports. \
Text imports now re-read their stored pasted text (scraping/steps/extract_text.rs stands in for extract_recipe when the job holds a source_text output). \
Do the same for photo imports: keep the photo ids the import read (the job's photo_extract input) as the source, and have Re-extract run vision extraction on them again before parse_ingredients, falling back to re-parsing when the photos are gone. \
API tests with the mock vision response first; no data/ diffs expected.",
